# Keep shell scripts LF, whatever the machine committing them does.
#
# A CRLF shebang is not a valid interpreter path -- "#!/usr/bin/env bash\r"
# asks for an interpreter literally named "bash\r" -- so a hook rewritten with
# Windows line endings stops running. The pre-commit PII scan fails that way
# quietly, which is the worst way for a guard on a public repo to fail.
.githooks/* text eol=lf
*.sh        text eol=lf
